Orbit Wars Simulator (Python vendored copy)
=============================================

This subdirectory (`simulator/python/orbit_wars_vendor/`) is a verbatim copy of
the `kaggle_environments/envs/orbit_wars/` directory from the
Kaggle/kaggle-environments project.

Source:
  https://github.com/Kaggle/kaggle-environments/tree/master/kaggle_environments/envs/orbit_wars

PyPI package version vendored: kaggle-environments 1.28.0
License: Apache License, Version 2.0 (see ./LICENSE)

Files vendored:
  orbit_wars_vendor/orbit_wars.py
  orbit_wars_vendor/orbit_wars.json
  orbit_wars_vendor/orbit_wars.js
  orbit_wars_vendor/README.md
  orbit_wars_vendor/tests/test_orbit_wars.py

This vendored copy is used in two ways within the Orbit Wars repository:

  1. As the reference implementation for the Rust simulator
     (`simulator/rust/`), to validate parity (state hash equivalence)
     between Python and Rust per-step.
  2. As a runtime fallback when `ORBIT_WARS_BACKEND=python` is set; in
     that mode the Python facade in `simulator/rust/python/orbit_wars_rust/`
     dispatches to this vendored interpreter rather than to Rust.

No modifications have been made to the vendored files. To upgrade:

  1. Bump kaggle-environments in `bot/pyproject.toml`.
  2. Re-copy the four files above from
     `<venv>/lib/python3.13/site-packages/kaggle_environments/envs/orbit_wars/`.
  3. Update the version line in this NOTICE.
  4. Re-run `pytest simulator/python/orbit_wars_vendor/tests` and the
     parity test in `simulator/rust/python/tests/test_parity.py`.
